DIFF contract_revision.meaning
  after : revision modes of the declared contracts (contract spec C06.2): a pinned contract (the default) is in force only where its contract text is the one pinned and the audited source matches one of the identities its lock records, each reviewed at a named revision, and every mismatch is withheld, so each call relying on it is held with reason code `contract-pin-mismatch`, and a function whose only unresolved diagnostics are held calls is Pending, never Safe; a flexible contract binds by name and declared signature only: on a function whose body this run analysed it is checked against that body as usual, and on a trusted function it is an explicit assumption of this run; every flexible libc contract without an analysed body is one standing assumption; held counts are recorded held-call refusals, a lower bound on textual call sites
  before: revision modes of the declared contracts (contract spec C06.2): a pinned contract (the default) is in force only where its contract text is the one pinned and the audited source matches one of the identities its lock records, each reviewed at a named revision, and every mismatch is withheld, so each call relying on it is Unknown with reason code `contract-pin-mismatch`; a flexible contract binds by name and declared signature only: on a function whose body this run analysed it is checked against that body as usual, and on a trusted function it is an explicit assumption of this run; every flexible libc contract without an analysed body is one standing assumption; held counts are recorded held-call refusals, a lower bound on textual call sites
DIFF pending_human_review.meaning
  after : declared contracts, or clauses of them, marked `resource_review_pending` (contract spec C06): each is loaded and validated but withheld, discharges nothing and accuses nothing, and every call site that would apply it is held with reason code `awaiting-human-review`, and a function whose only unresolved diagnostics are held calls is Pending, never Safe; a clause-level marker holds exactly the call sites a contract-level one does, because a contract is applied as one conjunction; `held_functions` counts analysed functions with at least one recorded held call of the declaration, and `held_call_sites` counts the held-call refusals the analysis recorded; the analysis of a path stops at its first refused statement, so a later call site on the same path records no refusal of its own and the count is a lower bound on textual call sites
